  "raw_text": "230\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb100\n):\n \nTimoti ba muihni nani ra kasak latwan kaiki kan bara piu sut ra hilp munaia want kan\n \n–\n \nTimothy was really\nloving the brothers and always wanted to help them\n \n/ Timoteo realmente amaba a los hermanos y siempre quiso\nayudarlos)\n\nSut ba\n \n–\n \nall the\n \n/ todos\n \nlos/la\ns\n\nSut kat\n \n–\n \ncompletely, entirely, altogether\n \n/ completamente, enteramente, en total\n\nWâlsut\n \n(a/t:\n \nWâl sut\n)\n \n–\n \nboth, the two together\n \n/ ambos, los dos juntos\n\nSutki\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntwin\n \n/ gemelo\n\nSwahni\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nsour\n \n/ ácido, agrio\n\nSwakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto strip off the skin, to peel\n \n/ quitar la piel, pelar\n\nSwaki sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto save\n \n/ salvar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmy49\n):\n \nSwaki wan saks!\n \n–\n \nSave us!\n \n/ ¡Salvanos!)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb84\n):\n \nDawan swaki ai saks!\n \n–\n \nLord save me!\n \n/ Señor, sálvame!)\n\nSwaki sakan lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsalvation\n \n/ salvación\n\nSwaki sakanka mana\n \n(\ndbta-Matiu 20:28)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nransom\n \n/ rescate\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nPri sakaia\nmana\n)\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \nkm-2012-15 translate ransom\n \nas\n \nAtki sakaia lâka\n;\n \nfg\n \ntranslates as\n \nPri sakaia ba;\n \nbh\n \ntranslates as\n \nPri\nsakaia pura mana ba;\n \ndb-Matiu 20:28\n \ntranslates as\n \nPri sakaia mana\n \n/\n \nkm-2012-15\n \ntraduce\n \nrescate\n \ncomo\n \nAtki\nsakaia lâka\n;\n \nfg\n \nse traduce como\n \nPri sakaia ba\n;\n \nbh\n \nse traduce como\n \nPri sakaia pura mana ba\n;\n \ndb-Matiu 20:28\n \nse\ntraduce como\n \nPri sakaia mana\n)\n\nSwaki sasakra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nsavior, liberator, deliverer, rescuer\n \n/ salvador, libertador, rescatador\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb77\n):\n \nNaha waitnika ra walan ningkara, pain wan dara walisa witin sika tasba swaki sasakrika aihwa ba\n \n–\n\nAfter (we)\n \nlistened to this man, we really feel that he truly is the real savior\n \n/ Después de que (nosotros)\n\nescuchamos a este hombre, realmente sentimos que él ciertamente es el verdadero salvador\n)\n\nSwaki sasakra daknika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nrescue team\n \n/ equipo de rescate\n\nSwak takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto escape\n \n/ escapar\n\n(Note\n/Nota\n: It seems that\n \nSwak takaia\n \nis more of a\n \ntrans\nitive\n \nform than\n \nSwakwi takaia\n \ndescribing something purposeful\n\nwhereas\n \nSwakwi takaia\n \nseems just to refer to the escape happening and doesn’t necessarily imply\n \npurpose\nful intent\n. /\n\nParece que\n \nSwak takaia\n \nes más una forma transitiva que\n \nSwakwi takaia\n \nque describe algo con un propósito, mientras\n\nque\n \nSwakwi takaia\n \nparece simplemente referirse al hecho de que se está escapando y no necesariamente implica una\n\nintención intencional.)\n\nSwakwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto escape, to be saved, to miss, to make a mistake, to go wrong\n \n/ escapar, ser salvo, fallar, cometer un\nerror, equivocarse\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmy59\n):\n \nwindarku swakwaia\n \n–\n \nto escape through the window\n \n/ escapar por la ventana)\n\nPlapi swakwi\n \n(\nmy4\n9) (v)\n \n–\n \nescaping by running\n \n/ escapar corriendo\n\nSwakwanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmistake, sin,\n \noffense,\n \ncrime, escape\n, defect\n \n(mwb\n-\n11/20)\n \n/ error, pecado,\n \nde\nlito,\n \ncrimen, fuga\n,\n\ndefecto\n \n(mwb\n-\n11/20)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-2 Timoti 3:16\n):\n \nswakwanka nani ba wapni daukaia\n \n–\n \nto make mistakes right; to set things straight\n \n/ corregir los\nerrores; arreglar las cosas)\n\nSwakwi takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto escape\n \n/ escapar\n\n(Note/Nota: It seems that\n \nSwak takaia\n \nis more of a transitive form than\n \nSwakwi takaia\n \ndescribing something purposeful\nwhereas\n \nSwakwi takaia\n \nseems just to refer to the escape happening and doesn’t necessarily imply purpose\nful intent. /\nParece que\n \nSwak takaia\n \nes más una forma transitiva que\n \nSwakwi takaia\n \nque describe algo con un propósito, mientras\nque\n \nSwakwi takaia\n \nparece simplemente referirse al hecho de que se está escapando y no necesariamente implica una\nintención intencional.)\n\nSwamp\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nswamp\n \n/ pantano\n\nSwampkira\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nswampy, muddy\n \n/ pantanoso, fangoso\n\nSwapaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nSwapkaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto tire, to be fatigued, to be exhausted, to become weak\n \n/ cansarse, estar\nfatigado, estar agotado, debilitarse\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nYang swapri\n \n–\n \nI am tired\n \n/ Estoy cansado)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nlfb\n-\n47\n):\n \nElías\n \nswapan pali kan bara dus kum\n \nmunhtara yapan\n \n–\n \nElijah was exhausted and slept under a tree\n \n/ Eli\ná\ns\n \nestaba\n\nagotado y dormía debajo de un árbol\n)\n\nDanh swapaia\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nKupia swapaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto give up, to tire out\n \n/ rendirse, cansarse\n\nDring\n \n(a/t:\n \nDrinh\n)\n \nswapaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto get tired, to get weary, to become exhausted\n \n/ cansarse, agotarse\n\nDring\n \n(a/t:\n \nDrinh\n)\n \nswapras\n \n–\n \nnot tired, not weary, not exhausted\n \n/ no cansado, no agotado, sin cansancio",
